# Sutich Stack HA – Privacy Policy

Last updated: November 20, 2026

Sutich Stack HA ("the app") is a private, single-user application run
by its developer and only user, Dewey (dewey72@gmail.com), as part of
his personal Home Assistant installation. Its purpose is described at
https://dewcifer.github.io/sutich-stack-ha/

## Data the app accesses
When the owner signs in with Google, the app requests access to:
- Google Calendar: event titles, times and calendar names.
- Google Tasks: task lists and tasks, which the app can read and update.
The app does not access Gmail, Drive, contacts, location or any other
Google data.

## How the data is used
Calendar and Tasks data is used only to give the owner schedule
announcements, reminders and synchronized to-do/grocery lists inside his
own home automation system. It is not used for advertising, analytics,
profiling or any purpose other than these features.

## Storage and security
- The app stores only the OAuth tokens needed to stay connected.
- Tokens and any cached Calendar or Tasks data are stored locally on a
  server in the owner's home. They are not copied to any external
  database or cloud service operated by the developer.
- The owner's Home Assistant instance is protected by authentication
  and network controls.

## Sharing and disclosure
The app does not sell, rent, share or transfer Google user data to any
third party. Data is disclosed only if required by law.

## Google API Services User Data Policy
Sutich Stack HA's use and transfer of information received from Google
APIs adheres to the Google API Services User Data Policy, including the
Limited Use requirements.

## Retention and deletion
Cached data is kept only while the integration is connected. The owner
can disconnect the integration at any time, which deletes the stored
tokens and cached data, and can revoke access at
https://myaccount.google.com/permissions

## Changes
Updates to this policy will be posted on this page with a new date.

